  Okaiwa — default (English) string resources.

  All user-visible copy is funneled through this file and its values-fr/
  sibling. Keys follow the `screen_section_purpose` convention so a reader
  can locate a string by the surface that owns it. Strings are grouped by
  screen in the order the user encounters them during onboarding and use.

  Log messages, error discriminators, and dev-only mock data are NOT
  translated — they stay hardcoded in code, since they never reach the
  user. See CLAUDE.md for the scoping rules.
-->
